# Peugeot 206 five-door hatchback, 1998-2012.
#
# The car that put Peugeot back at the top of the European small-car market:
# 3,838 mm long, 1,652 mm wide, 1,426 mm high, 2,442 mm wheelbase; 1.1 to 2.0
# litre petrol and 1.4 to 2.0 diesel, with the GTi 180 at the top. Sold in
# Britain from launch in 1998 and kept on as the 206 Plus after the 207 arrived,
# so the model ran until 2012. About 8.4 million built worldwide, one of the
# most numerous cars of its generation on British roads.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peugeot_206
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Blue and Red were the common UK finishes across the
# run; the photographs show silver, which was the most common of all.
#
# Weight: 16 in total (black 5, silver 5, blue 3, red 3). The 206 volume in the
# parc is well evidenced (about 567,000 licensed in 2005), so the total is high
# for a four-colour model.
#
# Speed 170 km/h (1.6); comfort 105/340 (line). Class 2.
# Dates: 1998-2012 with a short road tail to about 2028.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/peugeot-206.blend. References:
# citycars/references/peugeot-206/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

